WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.578 --> 00:00:03.745
- Hi. Oh, don't pee on me.

00:00:05.817 --> 00:00:07.317
Hello, oh puppies.

00:00:09.415 --> 00:00:14.284
(upbeat music) (barking)

00:00:14.284 --> 00:00:15.960
Hey, I'm Demi Lovato and I'm hanging out

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:18.943
with some puppies while
answering your questions.

00:00:18.943 --> 00:00:20.973
How am I supposed to
start answering questions?

00:00:20.973 --> 00:00:23.140
Oh, you're so cute. Hello.

00:00:25.787 --> 00:00:28.449
You're a boy, I just found that out.

00:00:28.449 --> 00:00:32.487
I like the brown ones. They're playful.

00:00:32.487 --> 00:00:33.771
Can you describe your new album,

00:00:33.771 --> 00:00:35.341
Tell Me You Love Me, in three words?

00:00:35.341 --> 00:00:38.258
No, no. (laughter)

00:00:39.118 --> 00:00:42.035
My album in three words would be...

00:00:43.801 --> 00:00:47.634
vulnerable, raw and
soulful. Here we go, nope.

00:00:50.108 --> 00:00:52.687
Would you release a song
in Spanish in the future?

00:00:52.687 --> 00:00:54.003
If so, which Latin artist would

00:00:54.003 --> 00:00:55.826
you like to collaborate with?

00:00:55.826 --> 00:01:00.602
I actually, oh those are my
pants, those are my pants.

00:01:00.602 --> 00:01:04.199
No, honey. You will have to
wait and find out because I

00:01:04.199 --> 00:01:08.366
recorded something recently
that I think you will like.

00:01:10.599 --> 00:01:12.815
Oh my god. (laughter)

00:01:12.815 --> 00:01:15.972
Why did you decide to name
your album Tell Me You Love Me?

00:01:15.972 --> 00:01:18.556
I decided to name my
album Tell Me You Love Me

00:01:18.556 --> 00:01:21.290
because it's one of my
favorite songs off of the album

00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:25.275
and it also is a very
vulnerable and raw title.

00:01:25.275 --> 00:01:29.442
Oh no, he peed on his face. (laughter)

00:01:31.508 --> 00:01:33.591
You want bones? Bone? No?

00:01:36.303 --> 00:01:38.161
How is this album different than

00:01:38.161 --> 00:01:41.054
Confident or any of your other albums?

00:01:41.054 --> 00:01:42.342
This album is different than my

00:01:42.342 --> 00:01:44.724
other albums because it's more soulful,

00:01:44.724 --> 00:01:45.786
and I think it's the most mature

00:01:45.786 --> 00:01:48.044
out of all the albums that I've made.

00:01:48.044 --> 00:01:49.944
And I've done a lot of
growing up personally

00:01:49.944 --> 00:01:54.111
and professionally so I think
that that's the reason why.

00:01:55.019 --> 00:01:57.691
Are you gonna help me read the question?

00:01:57.691 --> 00:02:00.522
I recently just got out of
a long-term relationship.

00:02:00.522 --> 00:02:03.508
I was wondering how you
deal with a breakup.

00:02:03.508 --> 00:02:08.208
I deal with a breakup by
leaning on my closest friends

00:02:08.208 --> 00:02:11.541
and by getting out into
the dating scene again.

00:02:11.541 --> 00:02:15.081
I think that it's important
not to dwell on certain things

00:02:15.081 --> 00:02:18.530
and just to get back
out there and have fun.

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:21.697
(laughter) Oh my god.

00:02:22.899 --> 00:02:26.232
These are my pants and that's my finger.

00:02:27.912 --> 00:02:32.079
And that's my next question. (laughter)

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:40.859
Are you planning on
directing... (laughter)

00:02:40.859 --> 00:02:43.601
Are you planning on directing
more of your music videos

00:02:43.601 --> 00:02:45.897
like how you directed Made in the USA?

00:02:45.897 --> 00:02:48.804
I think I would love to
direct at some point,

00:02:48.804 --> 00:02:52.014
but maybe the next one, who knows?

00:02:52.014 --> 00:02:53.770
You've had such an amazing career so far.

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:55.105
What has been your best achievement?

00:02:55.105 --> 00:02:58.272
I think having a number one single was

00:03:00.206 --> 00:03:01.725
definitely a career highlight and

00:03:01.725 --> 00:03:04.558
also getting my Grammy nomination.

00:03:07.589 --> 00:03:10.525
(laughter) What's your
favorite tattoo that you have

00:03:10.525 --> 00:03:12.361
and are you planning on getting more?

00:03:12.361 --> 00:03:15.135
I'm not planning on getting more as of

00:03:15.135 --> 00:03:18.564
right now, but that'll change I'm sure.

00:03:18.564 --> 00:03:22.064
My favorite tattoo is my lion on the hand.

00:03:23.729 --> 00:03:25.246
You're an inspiration to your fans and to

00:03:25.246 --> 00:03:27.080
other people who have
gone through tough times.

00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:28.902
What does it mean to you
to be able to inspire

00:03:28.902 --> 00:03:33.697
and change the lives of
others through your fame?

00:03:33.697 --> 00:03:35.280
I think that it's really important

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:38.197
that you use your platform for good

00:03:39.859 --> 00:03:44.026
and if I've been able to
use my tough times and...

00:03:45.885 --> 00:03:47.052
use them as...

00:03:49.545 --> 00:03:52.807
There's puppies. I don't
know. There's puppies.

00:03:52.807 --> 00:03:55.525
I think that if I'm able
to use the difficult times

00:03:55.525 --> 00:04:00.229
that I've been through as
lessons for other people,

00:04:00.229 --> 00:04:03.646
then I think I'm happy to inspire others.

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:09.086
Nope, those are my questions.

00:04:09.086 --> 00:04:10.340
What song on your newest album

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:12.324
do you think is the most personal?

00:04:12.324 --> 00:04:16.902
I think the most personal
song on this album is

00:04:16.902 --> 00:04:20.057
either You Don't Do It For
Me Anymore or Ready For Ya.

00:04:20.057 --> 00:04:24.013
I think Ready For Ya
is a song that I wrote

00:04:24.013 --> 00:04:28.696
that explains a lot about a
breakup that I went through.

00:04:28.696 --> 00:04:30.441
After watching your cover of Silent Night

00:04:30.441 --> 00:04:31.819
I couldn't help but think would you ever

00:04:31.819 --> 00:04:33.735
consider making a Christmas album.

00:04:33.735 --> 00:04:36.412
I have considered making
a Christmas album.

00:04:36.412 --> 00:04:38.906
Hopefully I'll do that
soon. You never know.

00:04:38.906 --> 00:04:41.316
Social media can be really
tough on a person mentally.

00:04:41.316 --> 00:04:43.871
Any tips on staying sane
and confident in a world

00:04:43.871 --> 00:04:47.274
where every photo is
FaceTuned and Photoshopped?

00:04:47.274 --> 00:04:49.322
Well, I think that
learning to love yourself

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:51.905
is very important and
learning to love yourself

00:04:51.905 --> 00:04:54.182
in the skin that you're
in is very important.

00:04:54.182 --> 00:04:55.888
It can be difficult at times and of course

00:04:55.888 --> 00:05:00.133
the pressures are high
but I think that as long

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:02.460
as you love yourself
that's all that matters.

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:07.103
What's the most funniest, the
most funniest, memorable prank

00:05:07.103 --> 00:05:09.677
you've ever pulled and
who did you pull it on?

00:05:09.677 --> 00:05:13.168
The funniest prank that
I ever pulled on somebody

00:05:13.168 --> 00:05:17.906
was I pulled a prank on my
security guard and in Vegas

00:05:17.906 --> 00:05:20.506
it's legal to hire a lady of the night

00:05:20.506 --> 00:05:23.443
to make surprise visits for somebody.

00:05:23.443 --> 00:05:25.110
So I did that and...

00:05:26.966 --> 00:05:30.316
I sent her to my security
guard's room and told her

00:05:30.316 --> 00:05:33.533
to be very forceful and
make herself enter the room.

00:05:33.533 --> 00:05:37.736
And she did just that
and he was very startled

00:05:37.736 --> 00:05:40.687
and I'm glad that he didn't keep her.

00:05:40.687 --> 00:05:41.927
Which song on this record was the

00:05:41.927 --> 00:05:43.717
hardest to write slash record?

00:05:43.717 --> 00:05:46.132
The hardest song to record
was Smoke and Mirrors,

00:05:46.132 --> 00:05:48.450
which is on the deluxe
version of the album.

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:52.200
It was a very emotional
song that I wrote on,

00:05:53.267 --> 00:05:57.434
that basically reminded me,
what are you doing back there?

00:05:58.418 --> 00:06:01.767
That's my elbow. What are you doing?

00:06:01.767 --> 00:06:03.600
That reminded me of...

00:06:04.694 --> 00:06:08.232
some very emotional times
that I went through.

00:06:08.232 --> 00:06:10.245
Do you want to act again?

00:06:10.245 --> 00:06:13.053
I think I would love to act at some point,

00:06:13.053 --> 00:06:15.131
I've just been so focused
with music right now

00:06:15.131 --> 00:06:17.881
that I haven't had the chance to.

00:06:19.902 --> 00:06:23.444
What has been your favorite
fan interaction or experience?

00:06:23.444 --> 00:06:25.916
I haven't had a favorite fan experience

00:06:25.916 --> 00:06:27.707
because all of them are so special.

00:06:27.707 --> 00:06:29.899
I think that any time a fan tells me

00:06:29.899 --> 00:06:34.066
that I've saved their life
is extremely meaningful and

00:06:36.100 --> 00:06:38.961
it just matters so much to me and it's

00:06:38.961 --> 00:06:42.277
kind of unfathomable, so
it really means a lot.

00:06:42.277 --> 00:06:44.244
Last question. Who's the first person

00:06:44.244 --> 00:06:46.778
you call when you have good news?

00:06:46.778 --> 00:06:48.575
The first person I call is either

00:06:48.575 --> 00:06:51.224
my mom or my best friend Marissa.

00:06:51.224 --> 00:06:54.350
It's definitely my mom, actually.
And then I call Marissa.

00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:57.623
But I tell them good news and
they get so excited for me

00:06:57.623 --> 00:07:00.735
cause they're so supportive
and I love them so much.

00:07:00.735 --> 00:07:04.463
Interviewing with puppies was so much fun.

00:07:04.463 --> 00:07:07.631
They are so adorable. I wish
I could take all of them home.

00:07:07.631 --> 00:07:11.717
But you actually can.
They are from North Shore

00:07:11.717 --> 00:07:14.989
Animal League America and they're all up

00:07:14.989 --> 00:07:17.874
for adoption so hashtag
get your rescue on.

00:07:17.874 --> 00:07:21.315
So that's all I have. I'm
gonna go play with puppies now.

00:07:21.315 --> 00:07:23.143
Because they're so adorable and

00:07:23.143 --> 00:07:26.226
they're very, very playful right now.

00:07:27.579 --> 00:07:29.329
Oh. Oh. Oh, so sweet.

